WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.236
"Is Soy Milk the Most Nutritious
Non-Dairy Milk?"

00:00:10.105 --> 00:00:13.690
There is a constellation
of new choices

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.359
in the dairy case these days,
from almonds to oats,

00:00:17.359 --> 00:00:21.480
such that major dairy corporations
are going out of business.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.119
But a set of recommendations
on healthy beverage choice

00:00:24.119 --> 00:00:26.980
from like 12 to 24 months
of age cautioned

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.750
that these plant-based milks are not
adequate nutritional substitutes

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:35.160
for dairy milk, with the exception
of fortified soy milk.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.640
The report and the press coverage
immediately triggered an outcry

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.270
from the medical community
for many reasons

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.350
including the concern around
conflicts of interests,

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:46.660
as several of these endorsing
organizations received funds

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:49.720
from the dairy industry, though
one such organization is accused

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:51.699
of trying to cover that fact up

00:00:51.699 --> 00:00:55.250
by removing the National Dairy
Council from their list of sponsors

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.449
immediately after
the report was released.

00:00:58.449 --> 00:01:01.250
But what about
the merits of the report?

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:04.600
Well, after weaning, milk
of any kind is not required

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:08.439
and really shouldn't be relied upon
as a main source of calories.

00:01:08.439 --> 00:01:11.549
Children will be fine with
water and healthy food.

00:01:11.549 --> 00:01:13.860
If you are going
to give kids milk,

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:15.950
there would seem
to be a better choice.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.590
Although cow's milk
is rich in calcium,

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:20.040
it does not appear
to clearly reduce fractures

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:23.650
and most plant-based milks on
the market have the same amount.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:26.260
More importantly, the consumption
of cow's milk carries risks

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:29.880
including a potential association
with type 1 diabetes onset,

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:32.579
anemia in toddlers,
lactose intolerance,

00:01:32.579 --> 00:01:35.049
cow's milk protein allergy,
and infantile colic.

00:01:35.049 --> 00:01:38.329
I've got a bunch of videos
on those topics.

00:01:38.329 --> 00:01:40.970
So the adverse effects from
just normal consumption

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:43.719
of cow's milk must be
compared against the risks

00:01:43.719 --> 00:01:46.110
from plant-based milks,
which are problematic

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:50.090
mainly when used inappropriately,
meaning like to the exclusion

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:53.110
of most other foods: diets that
are clearly inappropriate,

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.600
like the case of kwashiorkor
in Atlanta,

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:59.846
because his diet was
basically 99% rice milk.

00:01:59.846 --> 00:02:01.170
Plant-based milks
have the benefit

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:03.970
of being low in saturated fat,
free of cholesterol,

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:07.829
and though the protein content is
generally lower than in cow's milk,

00:02:07.829 --> 00:02:10.660
plant-based milks are said
to be richer in terms of fiber.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:13.760
That's technically true, since
cow's milk has zero fiber,

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:16.590
but the fiber contents of plant-
based milks are pretty pitiful,

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:19.060
certainly compared to the whole
foods from which they were derived.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:23.200
I mean, a cup of soybeans themselves
would have more than 10 grams,

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.830
but still soy milk is likely
the least processed

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.540
out of all plant-based milks.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.860
It's basically just soak,
crush, cook, and strain,

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:33.310
and is said to be the only
non-dairy milk that contains

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:36.000
the same amount
of protein as cow's milk.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.170
That may have once been true,

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:41.310
but now there's pea milk, which
is also comparable protein-wise.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:43.569
They all tend to have the same
calcium and vitamin D levels

00:02:43.569 --> 00:02:44.569
and fewer calories,

00:02:44.569 --> 00:02:48.620
as many as five times fewer
calories than cow's milk, in fact.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.790
Soy milk has the additional
benefit of reducing

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:55.120
breast cancer risk in girls and
normalizing development.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:56.970
Soy milk consumption
is also associated

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.430
with lower prostate
cancer risk in men.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:01.799
And interventional studies
suggest improved gut health

00:03:01.799 --> 00:03:04.400
by boosting the growth
of good bacteria.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.640
Soy milk has
anti-inflammatory effects,

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:08.680
lowering c-reactive protein levels,

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:12.519
has desirable effects on phosphorus
metabolism compared to cow's milk,

00:03:12.519 --> 00:03:15.840
significantly reduces free radical
DNA damage compared

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.879
to rice milk or cow's milk,

00:03:17.879 --> 00:03:19.780
prevents bone loss in
postmenopausal women

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.940
when put to the test,

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:26.480
and can improve
insulin resistance.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:28.400
Soy milk can help
with stroke rehab,

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.230
improving walking speed,
exercise endurance,

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.980
grip strength, and
muscle functionality,

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:35.860
as well as lower blood pressure
in men and women better

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:39.650
than cow's milk, not to mention
lowering your LDL cholesterol

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:43.280
as much as 25%
after just 21 days.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:47.629
It is quite clear that nutritionally
soy milk is the best alternative

00:03:47.629 --> 00:03:50.840
for replacing cow's milk
in the human diet.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:52.840
Yes, there are all
sorts of benefits

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:55.209
of plant-based versus
udder-based milks.

00:03:55.209 --> 00:03:58.650
No casein, cholesterol,
lactose, less saturated fat,

00:03:58.650 --> 00:03:59.930
actually has a bit of fiber,

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:03.980
but what about the specter
of anti-nutrients?

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:07.890
Is there even such
a thing as anti-nutrients?

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.299
Longstanding evidence suggests
that consuming a diet

00:04:10.299 --> 00:04:13.530
rich in plant-based foods plays
a significant role in prevention

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:17.530
and reduction of chronic diseases,
such as cardiovascular disease,

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:20.950
cancer, stroke, dementia,
diabetes, cataracts, and others.

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:23.650
Despite the need to increase
plant-food consumption,

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.410
there have been some
concerns raised about

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.950
whether they are beneficial
because of the various

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:31.280
so-called anti-nutrient
compounds they contain.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.350
It's true there are some
compounds when eaten

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:35.470
in high enough quantities --
especially when taken

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:38.560
in isolation -- that can
have adverse effects.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.810
Whole plant foods also contain
thousands of other compounds

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:43.380
in the food matrix,
though, many of which

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:47.028
counteract the potential
effects of the anti-nutrients.

00:04:47.028 --> 00:04:49.000
Plant-based diets are associated

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:52.009
with a reduced risk of lifestyle-
induced chronic diseases.

00:04:52.009 --> 00:04:54.091
The thousands of phytonutrients
they contain

00:04:54.091 --> 00:04:58.060
promote antioxidant defense,
for example, reduce inflammation.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.650
In some cases, what has been
referred to as anti-nutrients

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:04.160
may, in fact, be therapeutic
agents for various conditions.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:07.139
See, for example, my video
series on the role of phytates

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:09.639
in the prevention and
treatment of cancer.

00:05:09.639 --> 00:05:11.900
I don't want to end
without emphasizing

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:16.830
one of the plant-based pros:
no lactose.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:19.690
People don't understand that
the majority of adult humans

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:24.300
on Planet Earth are unable
to digest cow's milk.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:26.699
Throughout childhood, the enzyme
you have that breaks down

00:05:26.699 --> 00:05:29.710
the milk sugar lactose begins
to decline in most individuals

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:35.240
throughout the world, which makes
sense since milk is for babies.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:38.860
Why would we need to digest it
after weaning from the breast?

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:42.220
And so most people experience
symptoms like bloating,

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:43.940
abdominal pain, intestinal gas,

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.699
and watery stool, or even
nausea and vomiting.

00:05:46.699 --> 00:05:49.699
The global prevalence estimate
of lactose malabsorption

00:05:49.699 --> 00:05:51.780
is more than 2 out of 3 people;

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.910
in the United States,
it's more like 1 out of 3.

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:56.430
But 95% of Asians,

00:05:56.430 --> 00:06:00.340
60% to 80% of African Americans
and Ashkenazi Jews,

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:02.539
80% to 100 % of American Indians,

00:06:02.539 --> 00:06:07.000
and 50 to 80 % of Hispanics
have trouble digesting milk.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.940
It's really mostly those
of northern European origin

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:11.729
who can handle it
throughout adulthood.

00:06:11.729 --> 00:06:15.910
So to say everyone should drink
milk seems like an example

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:19.130
of racial bias in
federal nutrition policy.

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:23.090
It's like they're assuming everyone
is of Northern European descent.

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:26.430
Overall, about 75%
of the world's population,

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:28.580
including 25% of those
in the United States,

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:31.900
lose their lactase enzymes
after weaning.

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.979
To fight
the vitamin D disease rickets,

00:06:33.979 --> 00:06:38.210
they had to choose something in the
food supply to fortify with vitamin D.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:41.120
Choosing dairy is ironic,

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:44.270
since individuals of African ancestry,
because of their darker skin,

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:47.400
are at particularly high risk
for vitamin D deficiency,

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:51.320
yet most can't properly digest it.

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:53.190
But there is some good news.

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:54.940
For reasons like these,

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:57.630
Canada has recently removed
dairy as a separate food group

00:06:57.630 --> 00:06:59.580
in their national dietary guidance.

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:03.290
In 2019, the new Canada's
Dietary Guidelines and food guide

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:06.570
were released, having undergone
a thorough review and update

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:08.270
to emphasize the
importance of consuming

00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:10.250
more plant-based products.

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:12.569
Another major change was
the removal of dairy

00:07:12.569 --> 00:07:16.849
as a separate food group
with --- wait for it ---

00:07:16.849 --> 00:07:19.090
water included
as the beverage of choice.

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:20.419
What a concept.

00:07:20.419 --> 00:07:22.610
The attenuated emphasis
on dairy products

00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:25.169
and the increased focus on
plant-based foods in Canada

00:07:25.169 --> 00:07:28.449
were based on several parameters,
including the removal

00:07:28.449 --> 00:07:31.610
of industry-funded studies
from consideration

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:37.154
as part of the evidence base.

